This is indeed probably a stylistic difference. I'd rather die bravely 
storming the Castle than hang around in the main dungeon waiting to die 
of starvation or YASD, on the off chance that some random carrier of MR 
will show up. And if you use Elbereth, there's a very good chance that 
the Castle would be survivable. I've probably done it before, although I 
don't recall specifically.

At any rate, if I *chose* to use a lot of extra turns, either to 
overcome a major problem with an individual game or to build up my 
character to Survivability Beyond All Doubt, then I wouldn't complain if 
the designers of the game decided to ratchet up the difficulty at some 
point because I was choosing to use all that time. There's even an easy 
backstory rationale: The Lady is getting impatient.

